# Tools CLI Parameters

Companion to `.cursor/skills/tools-dev/SKILL.md` (authoritative for all `tools/` work). This rule is a focused CLI quick-reference when editing source under `tools/**/src/**`.

Packages under `tools/` share a config-first CLI model (`core_tools.config.apply_cli_overrides`).

## Two config tiers

| Tier | Examples | Override surface |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Semantic** (orchestration) | `planning.*`, `limits.*`, `agent_context.*`, `run.*`, `provider.*` | YAML + `--set` **only** — no mirrored `--param` flags |
| **Presentation** (invocation) | `observability.*`, `runtime.runs_dir` | YAML + `--set`; optional dedicated flags/env for frequent toggles |

Precedence:

- **Semantic**: defaults → YAML → `--set`
- **Presentation**: defaults → YAML → `--set` → explicit dedicated CLI flag (omitted flags do not override YAML/`--set`)

`--set` is exposed on `tdp run` and `tdp resume` only.

## Default: YAML + `--set`

Do **not** add a dedicated flag per config leaf. Examples:

```bash
# GOOD
tdp run --config cfg.yaml --set planning.max_depth=5
tdp resume --run abc --config cfg.yaml --set limits.planning.max_agent_turns=20
tdp run --config cfg.yaml --set observability.log_level=verbose

# BAD — flags that duplicate config paths
tdp run --max-depth 5 --max-agent-turns 20
```

When adding a configurable field:

- Add defaults in `config/defaults.py`
- Register the dotted path in `ALLOWED_OVERRIDE_PATHS`
- Extend `schema_docs.py` / README; reject unknown keys
- **Presentation** paths under `observability.*` are auto-included in `RESUME_PRESENTATION_ALLOWLIST`; new presentation sections need an update in `config/resume_policy.py`
- **Semantic** limit paths under `limits.*` map to `RESUME_EXECUTION_POLICY_ALLOWLIST` (also derived)
- TDD: write failing CLI test from expected exit/output first (`.cursor/skills/tdd/SKILL.md`), then implement; use in-process `run_cli([..., "--set", "path=value"])`

## When dedicated CLI flags are justified

Add a separate argparse flag only when `--set` is insufficient or the knob is not a config leaf:

| Category | Examples | Why not only `--set` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Command routing | `--run`, `--config`, `--check`, `--view`, `--until` | Selects behavior/target, not config values |
| Store bootstrap | `--runs-dir` | Resolved with env/config before store open (`TDP_RUNS_DIR`) |
| Output mode | `--stream-json` | Invocation transport, stored in `invocation.json`, not semantic config |
| Presentation toggles | `--log-level`, `--no-color`, `--no-agent-text` | Ergonomic overrides; wire in `invocation.py`, `default=None` |
| Agent operation args | `tdp agent plan snapshot --depth N` | Per-request API parameters, not resolved-config overrides |

Do not pass semantic config through argparse into `resolve_config` — use YAML or `--set`.

Presentation fields live in resolved config for YAML/`--set` but are excluded from resume contract/execution digests; persist invocation choices via `invocation.py` / `invocation.json`.

## Anti-patterns

```python
# BAD — flag per semantic config field
parser.add_argument("--max-depth", type=int)

# BAD — flag per presentation leaf when --set suffices
parser.add_argument("--notify-progress", action="store_true")

# GOOD — semantic via --set
run_parser.add_argument("--set", action="append", metavar="PATH=VALUE", ...)
# e.g. --set notifications.progress=true (after registering notifications.progress)
```
